{"RunId":"684e1bf8-7342-4f87-9efe-5b477a0f539c","Seq":25,"Kind":"NodeCompleted","Synthetic":true,"TimestampUtc":"2026-04-27T16:48:30.5989611Z","NodeId":"n_ym05bcg","NodeName":null,"Payload":{"nodeInstanceId":"f2455cf9-2770-4612-bde2-a32085d7e294","duration":"PT2M3.5588676S","inputData":{"triggerType":"WebHook","triggerTime":"2026-04-27T16:46:26.9788787Z","webHookMethod":"POST","webHookRoute":"/webhook/investigate-icm","bodyJsonSchema":"{\n   \u0022type\u0022: \u0022object\u0022,\n   \u0022required\u0022: [\u0022incidentId\u0022, \u0022serviceName\u0022, \u0022teamName\u0022, \u0022timestamp\u0022],\n   \u0022properties\u0022: {\n     \u0022incidentId\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022integer\u0022, \u0022format\u0022: \u0022int64\u0022 },\n     \u0022serviceName\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022string\u0022 },\n     \u0022teamName\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022string\u0022 },\n     \u0022timestamp\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022string\u0022, \u0022format\u0022: \u0022date-time\u0022 }\n   }\n }","messageType":"json","body.timestamp":"2026-04-27T16:46:22.618Z","body.incidentId":784334093,"body.serviceName":"","body.teamName":"","__webhookBody":"{\n  \u0022incidentId\u0022: 784334093,\n  \u0022serviceName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022teamName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022timestamp\u0022: \u00222026-04-27T16:46:22.618Z\u0022\n}"},"outputData":{"mode":"skill","backend":"copilot","model":"claude-sonnet-4.6","agentName":"open-icm","agentSummary":"","result":"---\n\n## ICM 784334093 \u2014 Investigation Summary\n\n### Overview\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Title** | [Watson Harmony] Spike in crashes \u2014 Azure Local Edge Observability (Cloud) |\n| **Severity** | Sev 3 |\n| **Status** | Active |\n| **Service / Team** | Azure Stack HCI / UpdateService |\n| **Owner** | jrodriguezga |\n| **Triggered** | 2026-04-27T16:46:22.618Z |\n\n---\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThis is a **Watson Harmony auto-incident** triggered by an anomalous spike in crash dumps. The spike was first detected on **4/22/2026 1:30 PM UTC** (5 days before the IcM was opened) in the **japaneast** region (56 dumps) but spread broadly.\n\nThe dominant failure patterns reveal **two independent root causes**:\n\n#### 1. \uD83D\uDD11 Permission/Access Regression (majority of crashes \u2014 ~163 of 381 dumps)\n| Bucket | Dumps | Location |\n|--------|-------|----------|\n| \u0060UnauthorizedAccessException (0x80070005)\u0060 in \u0060TraceEvent.dll!TraceEventSession..ctor\u0060 | 139 | ETW session creation \u2014 service denied OS-level ETW access |\n| \u0060UnauthorizedAccessException (0x80070005)\u0060 in \u0060UpdateService.Service.dll!UnityConfig.RegisterCaching\u0060 | 24 | Service startup \u2014 access denied registering cache |\n\n\u003E **Signal**: Error \u00600x80070005\u0060 = \u0060E_ACCESSDENIED\u0060. The UpdateService process (\u0060microsoft.azurestack.updateservice.winsvchost.exe\u0060) is being denied access to create ETW trace sessions and register caching at startup \u2014 strongly indicating a **service account permission regression**.\n\n#### 2. \uD83D\uDD17 Cluster API / Connectivity Failures (~149 dumps)\n| Bucket | Dumps | Location |\n|--------|-------|----------|\n| \u0060Win32Exception (0x80004005)\u0060 in \u0060ClusterApi.dll!SafeClusterHandle.OpenClusterHandle\u0060 | 113 | Unable to open cluster handle \u2014 likely cascading from permission failure |\n| \u0060ConnectionFailureException (0x80131500)\u0060 in \u0060Http.Client.Remoting.dll\u0060 | 36 | Internal service-to-service communication failures |\n\n#### 3. \u26A0\uFE0F UpdateService Core ArgumentException (~59 dumps)\n- \u0060ArgumentException (0x80070057)\u0060 in \u0060UpdateService.Core.dll\u0060 \u2014 invalid arguments likely caused by service starting in a degraded/partial state.\n\n---\n\n### Impacted Components\n\n| Component | Dumps |\n|-----------|-------|\n| \u0060microsoft.azurestack.updateservice.winsvchost.exe\u0060 | 381 |\n| \u0060agentlifecycleagenthost.dll\u0060 | 170 |\n| \u0060microsoft.diagnostics.tracing.traceevent.dll\u0060 | 146 |\n| \u0060microsoft.azurestack.common.infrastructure.http.client.remoting.dll\u0060 | 67 |\n| \u0060downloadservice.winsvchost.exe\u0060 | 36 |\n| \u0060edgecommonclient.dll\u0060 | 12 |\n\n**Hotspot region**: \u0060japaneast\u0060 (56 concentrated dumps)\n\n---\n\n### Timeline\n\n| Time (UTC) | Event |\n|------------|-------|\n| **4/22/2026 1:30 PM** | Crash spike begins \u2014 Watson detects anomalous dump volume |\n| **4/27/2026 4:46 PM** | IcM 784334093 auto-created by Watson Harmony |\n| **4/27/2026 9:47 AM PDT** | AI summary last refreshed; no bridge/mitigation yet |\n\nNo correlated Ev2 deployments were listed in the incident data, though a recent update rollout to \u0060japaneast\u0060 is the most likely trigger.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Mitigation Steps\n\n1. **Audit service account permissions** on affected HCI nodes \u2014 specifically verify the UpdateService account has:\n   - Permission to create ETW trace sessions (\u0060SeSecurityPrivilege\u0060 / ETW session rights)\n   - Access to cluster APIs (\u0060OpenCluster\u0060 Win32 handle)\n\n2. **Review recent deployments** to \u0060japaneast\u0060 around 4/21\u20134/22 that may have tightened LSA/ACL policies or changed service identity.\n\n3. **Check \u0060UnityConfig.RegisterCaching\u0060** in UpdateService \u2014 the access denied error at startup suggests the cache store (likely a protected registry key or named pipe) had its ACL changed.\n\n4. **Investigate \u0060agentlifecycleagenthost.dll\u0060** (170 dumps) \u2014 this agent manages process lifecycle; if it fails, cascading crashes in UpdateService are expected.\n\n5. **Escalate to japaneast** as a priority region, but verify other regions aren\u0027t catching up.\n\n6. **Resolve via Watson Portal**: Navigate to the Azure Watson Portal links in each bucket to mark fixed once the permission regression is identified and rolled back/patched.\n\n---\n\n\u003E \u26A0\uFE0F The incident is **Active** with no discussion or mitigation on record yet. The access-denied pattern across two independent modules (\u0060TraceEvent.dll\u0060 and \u0060UpdateService.Service.dll\u0060) is the highest-confidence root cause \u2014 a permissions regression should be the first investigation path.\n\n[OUTPUT:incidentFolder] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\n[OUTPUT:summary.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\summary.md\n[OUTPUT:discussion.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\discussion.md\n[OUTPUT:rca.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\rca.md\n[OUTPUT:metadata.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\metadata.md\n[OUTPUT:ai_summary.md]","ai.success":true,"ai.model":"claude-sonnet-4.6","ai.durationMs":112268,"ai.inputTokens":131251,"ai.outputTokens":3253,"incidentFolder":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093","summary.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\summary.md","discussion.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\discussion.md","rca.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\rca.md","metadata.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\metadata.md"},"globalVariables":{"body.timestamp":"2026-04-27T16:46:22.618Z","codeIssueFile":"","agentFolder":"E:\\work\\hub\\docs\\wiki","__webhookBody":"{\n  \u0022incidentId\u0022: 784334093,\n  \u0022serviceName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022teamName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022timestamp\u0022: \u00222026-04-27T16:46:22.618Z\u0022\n}","repoMdFile":"E:\\work\\hub\\docs\\wiki\\repos.md","body.incidentId":784334093,"rcaFile":"","metadataFile":"","body.serviceName":"","discussionFile":"","mitigationStepsFile":"","body.teamName":"","rootRepoFolder":"E:\\work","incidentId":0,"queryLoopCount":0,"applicableTsgFile":"","incidentFolder":"","etwEventsFile":"","summaryFile.md":"","queryScore":0,"issueListFile":""}}}
